  "projects": [
   {
    "title": "Decentratality",
    "description": "Decentratality features a demo that allows prospective restaurant/hospitality owners and employees to test the POS and financial management systems built into the web app from any computer with internet access. This Demo will have general financial management for payroll and other business costs, as well as a complete POS system that operates on chain to ensure customer data security, as well as a streamlined customer experience. The Demo will one day be connected to a rewards token linked to a presale for a live token that will be the governance token of decentratality once a funding goal has been achieved from the initial sale (details on website). \n\nDecentratalitys ultimate goal is to be a hub for all businesses to live under to allow them to grow together through tokenized reward systems, allowing relationships to be built, to ensure customer experience is always at the highest standard possible. On the other side of things, we also want to allow businesses an avenue into web 3, by streamlining the process of reward systems on a business by business basis. One day, we hope to see Businesses of all shapes and sizes worldwide utilizing Decentratality to offer their customers a “tradeable-on-chain” rewards token seamlessly through the web 2 style web-application. Obviously I am very early in production, and much funding is needed before government regulation conflicts can be handled, but I am fully committed to making Decentratality a reality. Project currently only works on desktop but mobile support is on the way!!!\n\nLink to project GitHub: https://github.com/Terriffictony10/my-portfolio.git",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Aug 2024 - Present"
   },
   {
    "title": "blockchain-developer-bootcamp",
    "description": "In this Project, I learned how to build a decentralized crypto-currency exchange, backend, and frontend, from scratch. The project was developed alongside a class taught by Dapp University. In the class, I learned how to write all of the testing scrips in unit test fashion to ensure that each element of the contract is working properly before we do anything crazy in react with it. On the React side, it is important to note the well-designed state in redux. I feel that I have a good understanding of how to satisfy the criteria of a good RESTful program. the link to the website has a security concern because it is created using fleek so the link will not add itself to linked-in properly but I will put it here     https://brief-umbrella-screeching.on-fleek.app/",
